{
  "type": "record",
  "name": "PayrollLiabilitiesPosted",
  "namespace": "id.co.nativeapp.events.employee",
  "doc": "Emitted by employee-service (ADR 0032, Track P phase P4) when a payroll_run transitions CALCULATED -> POSTED -- the THIRD event of the post() transaction (after PayrollPosted and every LaborCostAllocated bucket), in the SAME outbox transaction (rule 3). Carries the run's total employer-borne labor cost (the SAME sum LaborCostAllocated's buckets total to) split into WHO it is owed to: net wages to employees, PPh21 to the tax office, BPJS to the two BPJS bodies, and any other statutory/voluntary employee-borne deduction. Consumed by finance-service to book ONE balanced ad-hoc journal entry per run -- Dr LABOR_CLEARING (6900, re-classing the labor clearing leg LaborCostAllocated already posted there) / Cr one leg per non-zero liability bucket -- the clearing re-class design (ADR 0032) chosen over a single combined journal spanning both PayrollPosted and LaborCostAllocated, which would force finance to block on an event that may not have arrived yet. NO PII (rule 6): company-level bucket TOTALS only, never a per-employee amount. A bucket amount MAY be NEGATIVE (the December Art-17 PPh21 true-up refund month, ADR 0031 Track P phase P3): finance posts a negative bucket on the OPPOSITE side (a Dr leg for its absolute value) rather than a negative Cr, so the entry stays balanced under the JournalLine single-sided invariant (debit XOR credit, both strictly positive) -- see ADR 0032 for the full derivation.",
  "fields": [
    {"name": "payroll_run_id", "type": "string", "doc": "The payroll_run aggregate id (UUID as string); also the Kafka partition key."},
    {"name": "company_id", "type": "string", "doc": "The owning tenant / company id (UUID as string)."},
    {"name": "period", "type": "string", "doc": "The payroll period (YYYY-MM)."},
    {"name": "run_seq", "type": "int", "default": 1, "doc": "The run sequence for the (company_id, period, run_type). A higher run_seq supersedes lower ACTIVE runs of the SAME run_type -- the supersession signal finance keys on."},
    {"name": "base_currency", "type": "string", "doc": "The run's base (functional) ISO-4217 currency; every amount below is in this currency."},
    {"name": "employer_cost_total_minor", "type": "long", "doc": "The run's total employer-borne labor cost, minor units: gross_total_minor + employer_contribution_total_minor (the SAME sum LaborCostAllocated's buckets total to). This is the Dr leg of the finance liability entry (LABOR_CLEARING, 6900). Never a float."},
    {"name": "liabilities", "type": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "record", "name": "PayrollLiabilityBucket", "fields": [
      {"name": "liability_role", "type": "string", "doc": "One of NET_WAGES_PAYABLE, PPH21_PAYABLE, BPJS_KES_PAYABLE, BPJS_TK_PAYABLE, OTHER_DEDUCTIONS_PAYABLE -- the AccountRole finance resolves via role_account_map. An unrecognised role fails safe to the SUSPENSE account (money never dropped, HR-3)."},
      {"name": "amount_minor", "type": "long", "doc": "The bucket amount, minor units. Normally positive (posted as a Cr leg); MAY be negative for PPH21_PAYABLE in the December Art-17 true-up refund month, in which case finance posts it as a Dr leg for its absolute value. Never a float."}
    ]}}, "default": [], "doc": "The liability buckets which, together with employer_cost_total_minor as the balancing Dr leg, form a balanced double-entry journal entry: employer_cost_total_minor == net_total + PPh21 + BPJS-Kesehatan(EE+ER) + BPJS-Ketenagakerjaan(EE+ER) + other deductions. The producer asserts this identity before writing and never emits an unbalanced set. A zero-amount bucket is omitted by the producer."},
    {"name": "uses_illustrative_rules", "type": "boolean", "doc": "True if ANY resolved statutory rule feeding this run is an ILLUSTRATIVE_PLACEHOLDER -- mirrors PayrollPosted's flag."},
    {"name": "posted_at", "type": {"type": "long", "logicalType": "timestamp-millis"}, "doc": "When the run was posted (epoch millis) -- the same instant stamped on PayrollPosted and every LaborCostAllocated bucket of this run."},
    {"name": "run_type", "type": "string", "default": "REGULAR", "doc": "The payroll run type -- REGULAR today; THR lands in Track P phase P8. Supersession and the payroll_run_ledger control row are keyed on (company_id, period, run_type, run_seq), so a future THR run never supersedes a REGULAR run for the same period. Positioned at the RECORD END like PayrollPosted/LaborCostAllocated (P4 review W2 -- single-schema runtime decode: end-position additions fail fast on old bytes instead of misreading; moot for this brand-new event but kept consistent)."}
  ]
}
